  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with recurrent episodes of dizziness and presyncope in the setting of known sick sinus syndrome and atherosclerotic heart disease. Given the recent transient cerebral ischemic attack, continuous mobile cardiac telemetry is ordered to evaluate for potential arrhythmic causes of cerebral hypoperfusion and to optimize rate control. This service is medically necessary to identify the arrhythmic cause of the transient cerebral ischemic attack and to guide rate control in the setting of sick sinus syndrome and atherosclerotic heart disease."
